(7296265, 1137688, 83080, '<td valign="top">You may stir up the anti-water drop crowd, but I think this is a very appropriate subject for this technique and well executed.  As a constructive critique/observation, the focal plane seems too tight for sharpness through many of the drops, so I wonder what something closer to f18 would have produced (or perhaps the focal plane wasn''t parallel to the glass).  But on the other hand, having drops well out of the focal plane adds a different feel to the illusion of depth for this type of shot. Regardless, it works and I like your interpretation of the challenge.</td>', 'You may stir up the anti-water drop crowd, but I think this is a very appropriate subject for this technique and well executed.  As a constructive critique/observation, the focal plane seems too tight for sharpness through many of the drops, so I wonder what something closer to f18 would have produced (or perhaps the focal plane wasn''t parallel to the glass).  But on the other hand, having drops well out of the focal plane adds a different feel to the illusion of depth for this type of shot. Regardless, it works and I like your interpretation of the challenge.', '2014-12-28 14:34:25.000000', NULL, 1),
