(7297446, 1137679, 163081, '<td valign="top">Some remarks about your camera settings.<br/>You shoot in ISO 3200 and a shutter speed of 1/125. The subject is totally motionless, this allows you to shoot with slower shutter and smaller ISO (sharper images, not so grainy)   I would choose ISo 100 and 1/8 or even lower if using a tripod or posing the camera on a book. The aperture is ok for this type of shot...</td>', 'Some remarks about your camera settings.You shoot in ISO 3200 and a shutter speed of 1/125. The subject is totally motionless, this allows you to shoot with slower shutter and smaller ISO (sharper images, not so grainy)   I would choose ISo 100 and 1/8 or even lower if using a tripod or posing the camera on a book. The aperture is ok for this type of shot...', '2015-01-01 11:05:47.000000', NULL, 0),
